# (build 110) The Escape menu's AUDIO page. On the title, Escape; down five
# stops is AUDIO (its value: the synth that plays), C opens its page: SYNTH
# (CHIP, Q), MASTER and MUSIC (OFF, then -30 dB up to 0 dB a dB at a time).
# route_probe is built without Q, so Q shows NOT BUILT under it and the chip
# plays on -- the menu's AUDIO still says CHIP. Left and right step a value
# and stop at its ends; C steps on and goes round (0 dB to OFF). Escape or B
# goes back a page. docs/audio.md, "The AUDIO page". The route reads its own
# settings.json, never the player's; the probe has no main.c, so nothing is
# written here. The waits put the cursor's lamp in its lit half.
start new
wait screen title
press esc
expect escape-menu open
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
expect audio summary CHIP
wait ticks 12
shot menu_audio
press c
expect audio synth CHIP
expect audio master 0 DB
expect audio music 0 DB
wait ticks 10
shot page_default
# SYNTH: Q, which this build has not got; the chip still plays.
press right
expect audio synth Q / NOT BUILT
expect audio summary CHIP
wait ticks 8
shot page_q_not_built
press c
expect audio synth CHIP
# MASTER: right stops at 0 dB; left steps down a dB; C from 0 dB goes
# round to OFF, and on to -30 dB.
press down
press right
expect audio master 0 DB
press left
press left
press left
expect audio master -3 DB
press c
press c
press c
expect audio master 0 DB
press c
expect audio master OFF
press left
expect audio master OFF
press c
expect audio master -30 DB
press left
expect audio master OFF
press right
press right
expect audio master -29 DB
# MUSIC, a dB a press.
press down
press left
expect audio music -1 DB
press left
press left
press left
press left
press left
expect audio music -6 DB
wait ticks 8
shot page_volumes
# B back to the menu, the page's values kept; B again closes it.
press b
expect escape-menu open
expect audio summary CHIP
expect audio master -29 DB
press b
expect escape-menu closed
